WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.399 --> 00:00:08.259
Now that IT has been released on Blu-Ray,
we have access to some bonus content that

00:00:08.259 --> 00:00:12.769
can tell us even more about this world that
Andy Muschietti has created and more about

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:16.119
the haunting entity that resides inside of
Pennywise.

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:19.529
In this video I'll break down some of the
things you may have missed in the blu-ray

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:24.029
bonus content and I'll be discussing another
possible ending to the movie, so be sure to

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:25.439
stick around for that.

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:27.060
This is Things You Missed.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.160
The first bonus video is all about bringing
Pennywise to life and it includes interviews

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.890
with the kids about their experiences on set
with him.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:37.650
I found myself trying to figure out Ben's
wardrobe choice, which was a t-shirt that

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.970
features African safari animals.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:44.269
It's something I noticed when I did my original
Things You Missed videos when IT was in theaters,

00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:47.720
but didn't include because I hadn't deciphered
the meaning behind it.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.002
It wasn't until later in this documentary
that I think I finally figured it out.

00:00:51.002 --> 00:00:53.510
"Andy has a thing with spit and drool.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:59.460
Like I don't know what it is that appeals
him about spit, but there's something about

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.460
it that he loves.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.390
So I got a lot of drool on me."

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.240
"He's very drooly and he brought this to the
character and it's a great thing because he's

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.430
like Pennywise.

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.640
He gets hungry in the presence of scared children."

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.810
OK, this makes a lot more sense now.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.040
I went back and looked at the shirt again
and noticed that all these animals are the

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.040
prey.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:22.250
Just as predators of the African savanna might
salivate over their meals, Pennywise salivates

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.240
over the fear of children.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.330
This is also like 2 Things You Missed in one,
because everyone has their own individual

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:33.750
fears; Beverly has her father, Stanley has
his Bar-Mitzvah, but Eddie is a hypochondriac;

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.050
he's afraid of germs.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:39.720
He's the only one that Pennywise was drooling
on, thus making him more afraid, and in turn,

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.670
making Pennywise even hungrier.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.409
So the cycle repeats itself.

00:01:43.409 --> 00:01:47.170
There's also a behind the scenes shot of that
children's TV show that plays on many of the

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.720
TVs in Derry, "That's right.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.790
And you will too Henry.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.390
Make it a wonderful day.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:58.420
Kill him," where we can see essentially the
full unobstructed cast.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.619
You'll noticed that many of the children sitting
there are look like zombies.

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:05.921
My theory is that these kids are some of the
past and future victims of Pennywise, and

00:02:05.921 --> 00:02:08.920
once he devours them, they may appear on this
show.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:12.889
In addition to Ben's shirt, another thing
I noticed but didn't have an answer for when

00:02:12.889 --> 00:02:16.909
I first saw the movie, was this old-timey
tricycle in the 29 Neibolt House.

00:02:16.909 --> 00:02:21.120
I assumed that it was just there because it
looks circus-y and maybe even as a loose reference

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.120
to The Shining.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.299
However, in the other character video in the
bonus content we get a better look at Richie's

00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:27.889
shirt from the end of the movie.

00:02:27.889 --> 00:02:32.409
As I mentioned in a previous video, it reads
"Derry Bike and Cycle Shoppe" which plays

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:36.349
into the pattern of IT re-emerging on a cycle
of every 27 years.

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:39.439
The graphic on the shirt looks to be the same
tricycle from the house.

00:02:39.439 --> 00:02:43.840
We also see a doll version of Richie in the
house, and missing posters with Richie's face

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:44.840
on them.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.000
These are all clues that Richie was supposed
to die in this house, but he ends up surviving

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.590
anyway, making the other piece of text on
that shirt, "Life.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.292
Enjoy The Ride", all the more appropriate.

00:02:55.292 --> 00:02:59.239
The next video features Stephen King talking
about his inspirations for the book, and in

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:01.540
it we get a better look at the drain pipe.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.829
In most of the scenes it's very dark, but
here you can actually make out an etching

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:08.069
of a stick figure holding balloons.

00:03:08.069 --> 00:03:12.230
If only Patrick Hockstetter had seen that
before venturing into the sewer.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.739
On to the deleted scenes.

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:18.279
One of the scenes takes place in Henry Bowers
room, which is a canvas to his violent tendencies.

00:03:18.279 --> 00:03:23.489
It's filled with weapons, a road sign covered
in bullet holes and he even has a framed picture

00:03:23.489 --> 00:03:25.510
of a gun, which I find really funny...

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.139
The next one is in Beverly's room.

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:31.049
In my previous IT video I talked about the
significance of Bev's Siouxsie and the Banshees

00:03:31.049 --> 00:03:35.360
poster, and in this deleted scene, we get
to see a little bit more of her punk rock

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.169
collection, which includes a Psychedelic Furs
poster.

00:03:38.169 --> 00:03:41.040
This is a pretty deep reference, so stick
with me here.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.840
The Psychedelic Furs really got off the ground
when their song Pretty In Pink was featured

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.200
in the John Hughes movie with the same title.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.760
And if you've seen that 80s classic, you know
that it stars Molly Ringwald, which ties back

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.680
into IT with this line: "Cause I want to run
toward something.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:56.680
Not away."

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.680
"I'm sorry.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.370
Who invited Molly Ringwald to the group?"

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:01.370
"Richie..."

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.370
"I'm just saying."

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:05.590
Shortly after this there is an extended scene
where the Keene girl from the pharmacy signs

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:06.590
Eddie's cast.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.379
There are two things to take note of here.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:11.620
We get a clear shot of her necklace, showing
her name Gretta.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:16.030
That makes me think this character could be
a combination of Mr Keene's daughter and Gretta

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.230
Bowie from the book, who is a character who
bullies Beverly, as seen in the first school

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.549
scene in this movie.

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:25.560
The other detail was Gretta sticking her gum
on the cast at the end, which again plays

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.620
into the idea that this will really bother
Eddie because he's a hypochondriac.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:33.440
Now let's talk about the last of the deleted
scenes, which was originally supposed to be

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:34.590
the ending of the movie.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.590
In several of the deleted scenes there is
a subplot where Bill's family plans a vacation

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:42.410
to Acadia but the parents don't want to go
anymore after Georgie's death, because Georgie

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.380
was really looking forward to going there.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.139
So in this final deleted scene they set off
on a new family vacation to a new destination

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:53.770
as a symbolic moving on from the Georgie cloud
that hangs over this family's head.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:05:15.979
Then this happens.

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:19.919
I personally really like this ending as opposed
to it ending on Bill and Beverly's kiss.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:23.650
If I were to do it, I would take away the
growling sounds to preserve the mystery of

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.830
if IT was really defeated.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.520
Even though we know there's another movie
coming.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.560
But let me know which ending you like better
in the comments.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:34.150
I actually have one more Thing You Missed
but it does contain spoilers, so if you haven't

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:37.129
read the book, then you're gonna want to head
on over to another video, but please to remember

00:05:37.129 --> 00:05:40.510
to subscribe and ring that death bell for
notifications on your way out.

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:44.000
But for those of you who have read the novel,
it looks like we might me getting that epic

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.210
ending in the upcoming IT Chapter 2.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:50.349
Ben's room is filled with these Derry newspaper
clippings, but in the bonus features we get

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.590
a closer look at this one in particular.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:56.620
This is a page out of the 1937 Derry Courier
newspaper.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:06:01.449
This smaller article is titled, "Special Session
sets stage for Flood Control," just dropping

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:06.310
a small hint that Derry's strange sewer system
may be prone to flooding.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:10.939
Of course, the IT mini-series did drop a similar
hint, but then no flood scene was included,

00:06:10.939 --> 00:06:13.460
but I have a feeling we'll be seeing it this
time around.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.650
If that's something you'd like to see, go
ahead and give this video a like.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.129
My name is CZ and I also write horror here
on YouTube.

00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:23.030
And of course I'll be talking about the next
IT movie as soon as the trailer comes out,

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.150
as well as many of the other big horror movies
before then.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.150
Don't miss out on it.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.189
You know already know what to do.

00:06:28.189 --> 00:06:29.810
I'll see you in the next one.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:31.389
Assuming we both survive.

